      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This dose is double the immediate-release maximum. It would raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose or frequency.** For example, 500 mg or 1000 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily was intended, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
